{"kind":"stack","id":"s-human-dev","title":"Human development: from birth to old age","theme":{"background":"#fdf6e3","foreground":"#2d2d2d","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-q","content":"Which stage of life comes first?"},{"type":"button","id":"c1-a","label":"Babyhood","why":"Babyhood is the first stage, right after birth.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Old age","why":"Pupils may think the last stage starts the cycle, but it comes last.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-c","label":"Adulthood","why":"Pupils may forget childhood comes before adulthood.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Growth"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"Growth is getting bigger and taller as the body develops over time."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-n","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"During which stage do people usually learn to walk and talk?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"Toddler years","why":"Toddlers learn to walk and talk in their early years.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"Teenage years","why":"Pupils may think big changes in speech happen in the teens.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Old age","why":"Pupils may think people only learn new skills when young, mixing up direction.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-t","content":"You are in your garden and a friend asks you to climb a tree. What do you do?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Climb the tree","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Stay on the ground","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"You climb with care. Your strong, growing body helps you reach the top!"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-n","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"You stay down and read a book under the tree. Your friend climbs alone."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-n","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-q","content":"What usually happens to the body in old age?"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-a","label":"Bones and muscles can get weaker","why":"As people age, bones and muscles often become weaker.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Bones and muscles grow much bigger","why":"Pupils may think growth continues into old age, which it does not.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-c","label":"The body stops needing food","why":"Pupils may think the body needs less of everything, but it still needs food.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"What is the teenage stage called?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"Adolescence","why":"Adolescence is the stage of change between childhood and adulthood.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Infancy","why":"Pupils may mix up infancy, the earliest stage, with the teenage years.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"Maturity","why":"Pupils may confuse maturity, a later adult stage, with the teenage years.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-t","content":"Adulthood"},{"type":"text","id":"c9-e","content":"Adulthood is the stage when a person is fully grown and is responsible for their own life."},{"type":"button","id":"c9-n","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which stage comes just before old age?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"Adulthood","why":"Adulthood comes before old age in the life cycle.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Babyhood","why":"Pupils may forget babyhood is near the start of life, not the end.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Childhood","why":"Pupils may think childhood comes after old age, reversing the order.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"You finished the human development lesson!"},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Well done. You now know how people change from birth to old age."}],"actions":[]}}
